    "body": "## Description\n\nWhen a completed interaction A is followed by an unfinished request B, implicit terminal reward assignment currently targets B. Export then removes B, leaving A without a reward and potentially rejecting the entire rollout group. Assign the reward to the latest completed interaction instead, using the same completeness check as export.\n\nExclude unfinished entries from retry-orphan candidates so an unfinished duplicate cannot displace a completed response. Preserve existing parent-child consumption evidence. If no completed interaction exists, return an error and propagate implicit assignment failures to the caller. Explicit completion IDs and stream aliases retain their existing behavior.\n\n## Related Issue\n\nRelated to #1702 and #1746. No issue is closed by this PR.\n\n## Type of Change\n\n- [x] 🐛 Bug fix\n- [ ] ✨ New feature\n- [ ] 💥 Breaking change\n- [ ] 📝 Documentation update\n- [ ] ♻️ Refactoring\n- [ ] ⚡ Performance improvement\n- [ ] ✅ Test coverage improvement\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [ ] I have read the [Contributing Guide](https://github.com/areal-project/community/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [ ] Pre-commit hooks pass (`pre-commit run --all-files`)\n- [x] Relevant tests pass; new tests added for new functionality\n- [ ] Documentation updated (if applicable; built with `./docs/build_all.sh`)\n- [x] Branch is up to date with `main`\n- [ ] Self-reviewed via `/review-pr` command\n- [x] This PR was created by a coding agent via `/create-pr`\n- [ ] This PR is a breaking change\n\n## Additional Context\n\nValidation: 74 CPU tests passed after rebasing onto `0fa9f623`.\n\n```bash\npython -m pytest -q -m 'not slow' \\\n  tests/experimental/openai/test_completed_reward.py \\\n  tests/experimental/openai/test_cache.py \\\n  tests/experimental/openai/test_retry_orphan.py \\\n  tests/experimental/openai/test_proxy_rollout_server.py\n```\n\nThe two core regression cases fail on the unmodified implementation. Coverage includes unfinished tails and duplicate requests, repeated reward assignment, sessions without completed interactions, explicit IDs/aliases, and HTTP error propagation. Read-only code review completed. No GPU end-to-end validation is claimed.\n\nFull pre-commit was run. Static formatting, lint and license checks passed. Host configuration/CLI hooks are blocked by Python 3.10 / older PyTorch; corresponding scripts passed in the Python 3.12 target image. The lockfile hook could not fetch main's Megatron Bridge 0.6 wheel. No dependency or lockfile changes are included.\n\nThis patch addresses unfinished cached requests. Attribution to completed retry orphans and requests arriving after assignment remain separate lifecycle issues; it does not establish general concurrency safety or convert missing rewards to zero.\n",
